<title>UK: BFCE adds $100 million to perpetual step-up FRN.</title>
<headline>BFCE adds $100 million to perpetual step-up FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following step-up</p>
<p>floating-rate issue has been increased lead manager Morgan</p>
<p>Stanley said on Thursday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANQUE FRANCAISE DU COMMERCE EXTERIEUR</p>
<p> AMT    *$100 MLN     BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY ***PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN   **+75 BP    PAY DATE****13.FEB.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A2	  ISS PRICE  99.584    FULL FEES   0.50</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A	   REOFFER    99.584</p>
<p> NOTES	*ORIGINAL $150 MLN LAUNCHED 15.NOV.96</p>
<p>	     **TO DEC 2001, THEN +150 BP TO DEC 2006, THEN +225 BP</p>
<p>	    ***CALLABLE AT PAR DEC 2001</p>
<p>	   ****PLUS 63 DAYS ACCRUED INTEREST</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/UK/FR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.30	SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
